                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "448f4b6c-ea4d-324c-8029-bb188a6489ed",
                        "entry_id": "298bac40-5783-3c5b-845f-ce75e02620f8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "That which refreshes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aef530cd-b462-4544-a9b4-4c9d112e3b76",
                                "sense_id": "448f4b6c-ea4d-324c-8029-bb188a6489ed",
                                "text": "His auditors gaine so refreshed him, as to take away the sense of all paine in teaching. Their profit was his refectives and reparatives."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc5a1fc9-ae0d-4894-9c1a-f57b90a648ad",
                                "sense_id": "448f4b6c-ea4d-324c-8029-bb188a6489ed",
                                "text": "You should have refreshed our bowels, been as cordials, and sweet refectives, after all our wearisome labours: but have not you dealt unkindly with us?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25b32287-483d-45d0-85eb-ba237deb0a12",
                                "sense_id": "448f4b6c-ea4d-324c-8029-bb188a6489ed",
                                "text": "There is a cool and pleasant refective exceedingly agreeable in social parties, large or small, at all seasons of the year, and especially so in the hot weather of our long dry summers."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ed99f138-acff-3121-9fb9-e64150f0d284",
                        "entry_id": "298bac40-5783-3c5b-845f-ce75e02620f8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A type of animal that eats its food twice, by reconsuming partially digested matter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "110ba36a-6490-4904-94ad-5d7e0459d791",
                                "sense_id": "ed99f138-acff-3121-9fb9-e64150f0d284",
                                "text": "While the rabbits mentioned in Leviticus 11 appear to chew the cud, we now know that they are not, in fact, ruminants but technically \"refectives\" - that is , they chew their droppings to better digest their food, not cud like a cow."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
